OpenSSL: no aarch64 assembly code that writes x18.

XNU and Windows can change x18 at any time. The vpsm4 code of SM4 writes
x18, so the aarch64 build uses only sm4-armv8.S for SM4. Code that
writes x28, the thread pointer of Cosmopolitan Libc, keeps its assembly:
the libc gives a signal handler the thread pointer from its copy (C73,
cosmocc 4.0.2-patched.5). check_openssl_asm of scripts/steps.sh checks
the result. See C73 and SSL1 of docs/UPSTREAM.md.

diff --git a/crypto/sm4/build.info b/crypto/sm4/build.info
index 2f36b6b..a67376c 100644
--- a/crypto/sm4/build.info
+++ b/crypto/sm4/build.info
@@ -1,8 +1,10 @@
 LIBS=../../libcrypto
 
 IF[{- !$disabled{asm} -}]
-  $SM4DEF_aarch64=SM4_ASM VPSM4_ASM
-  $SM4ASM_aarch64=sm4-armv8.S vpsm4-armv8.S vpsm4_ex-armv8.S
+  # beam.com: XNU and Windows can change x18 at any time, and the vpsm4
+  # code writes x18. Thus only sm4-armv8.S, which does not use x18.
+  $SM4DEF_aarch64=SM4_ASM
+  $SM4ASM_aarch64=sm4-armv8.S
 
   $SM4DEF_riscv64=SM4_ASM
   $SM4ASM_riscv64=sm4-riscv64-zvksed.s
